Article 37
Every person related to the implementation of Protection of Women who knows of the occurrence of acts of Violence against Women but allows it, does not provide Protection to Victims, and/or does not report to the relevant agency may be subject to administrative sanctions in the form of:
a. written warning;
b. temporary suspension from activities;
c. termination of cooperation;
d. revocation of registration certificate;
e. revocation of operational permit;
f. withdrawal of facilities; and
g. administrative fine.

CHAPTER VIII
INSTITUTIONAL ARRANGEMENTS
Article 39
(1) P2TP2A organizes women's protection services.
(2) Women's protection services by P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) involve elements of:
   a. health;
   b. psychology;
   c. law;
   d. religious leaders;
   e. social; and
   f. economic.
(3) Further provisions regarding the establishment, membership composition, duties, and functions of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be stipulated by Regent's Decree.

